.TH SKOGAI-MODULE-NEW 1  "skogai-module-new 0.0.0" 
.SH NAME
skogai\-module\-new \- scaffold a new module from core's templates/module
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBskogai module new\fR [OPTIONS] <NAME> [DESCRIPTION]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-to\fR=\fITO\fR
.br
where to create it, default core.module.install
.br

.br
[\fIpossible values: \fRlocal, global]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
Print help
.TP
<\fINAME\fR>
.br
lowercase, one segment
.TP
[\fIDESCRIPTION\fR]
.br
what it is, one line
.SH "ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES:"
.TP
\fISKOGAI_SYSTEM_DIR\fR [default: /etc/skogai]
.br
dir of the system layer config
.TP
\fISKOGAI_CONFIG_DIR\fR
.br
dir of the global layer, default ~/.config/skogai
.TP
\fISKOGAI_LOCAL_DIR\fR [default: .skogai]
.br
dir of the local layer; relative is from the git root, or pwd
.TP
\fISKOGAI_MODULE_PATH\fR
.br
colon\-separated dirs of module sources, default the one this module sits in
